2026-07-10T06:54:07.9206846Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9207313Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9207679Z     
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9207874Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9208119Z     
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9208308Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9208529Z     
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9208723Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9208979Z         def inc(x):
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9209187Z             return x + 1
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9209418Z     
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9209587Z     
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9209852Z         def test_answer():
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9210187Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9210537Z     
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9210940Z     
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9211199Z     To execute it::
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9211491Z     
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9211783Z         $ pytest
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9212149Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9212580Z         collected 1 items
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9225048Z     
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9225485Z         test_sample.py F
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9225736Z     
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9225995Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9226427Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9226760Z     
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9226952Z             def test_answer():
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9227194Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9227447Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9227690Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-07-10T06:54:07.9227923Z     
